Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.17,0:00:07.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The toll counter is back:\Nevery car is now {\c&HF09CB4&}generated{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.68,0:00:10.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}They come from the machine\Nwith the built-in mirror:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.82,0:00:12.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}twenty thousand at each of forty-one
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.99,0:00:15.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}settings of {\c&H7AAF1B&}Gamma{\c&HF7F4F2&},\Nmost unseen in training.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.39,0:00:20.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Rice, with the equations,\Nturns them into a {\c&H00A1ED&}crossing rate{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.22,0:00:24.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Against the counted truth,\Nfar from the threshold,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.42,0:00:27.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the {\c&H00A1ED&}cumulative error{\c&HF7F4F2&} is fourteen percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.81,0:00:31.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Setting by setting, the miss\Naverages seventeen percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.43,0:00:34.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}and reaches sixty-five\Npercent at two settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.37,0:00:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Near the threshold, the error\Nclimbs to forty-two percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.09,0:00:42.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One model, one training seed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.80,0:00:46.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Rice needs the equations,\Nand gives a rate, not waiting times.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.45,0:00:51.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So, the study's third question:\Ncan a machine tell us {\c&H00A1ED&}how often{\c&HF7F4F2&}?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.33,0:00:58.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}For crossings on three dials: far from the\Nthreshold, roughly yes; near it, not yet.
